      "activity_description": "Add a `syncable` boolean option to the HDFS sink; when enabled, call hsync()/hflush() after each record write to provide durability in case of sink/container failure. Plumb the option through the sink's configuration and serialization paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U4 - HDFS syncable writes: testing",
      "activity_description": "Add tests that simulate container/sink failure mid-write with sync enabled and verify data durability and behavior trade-offs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U5 - HDFS direct filename: design and implementation",
      "activity_description": "Add a `useDirectFilename` (or equivalent) option to the HDFS sink that skips the `.tmp` inUseSuffix and writes directly to the target file. Ensure interaction with U4 (syncable) is well-defined.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - HDFS direct filename: testing",
      "activity_description": "Add tests verifying the sink writes to the target filename (no .tmp file) and that recovery after mid-write failure behaves correctly when combined with the syncable option.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Maven/Gradle module upload: design",
      "activity_description": "Design Maven (`maven-xd-plugin`) and Gradle (`gradle-xd-plugin`) plugins that expose an `uploadModule` goal/task wrapping Spring XD's module registration REST API. Define the parameters (admin URL, credentials, module coordinates, properties file).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Maven/Gradle module upload: implementation",
